## Context

Author decision (2026-06-12): the paper no longer discusses
pre-registration. Experiment 2 is presented as a plain 2×2 factorial —
query mode (naive / optimised) × documents (no / yes), four agents, N=5
per cell, 80 sessions — all arms on equal footing. No "registered vs
unregistered", no "exploratory because unregistered", no "as-run
deviations from the registration". Real facts carried by those sentences
(sequencing of the two batches, the judge-vendor change, exclusions,
Phase C deferral) survive as plain design description.

Reviewer line numbers below were verified on main 79d3cba3 — re-locate
by grep/label before editing (line hints die fast across merges).

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.tex` — all sites below
- `tests/test_manuscript_exp2_annex_as_run.py` — pins the old vocabulary
- `docs/editorial-brief.md` — sweep for registration vocabulary in
  entries; update wording (decisions themselves unchanged)

## Actions (per-site plan; quotes abbreviated, grep to relocate)

1. ~L736-739 table caption `tbl:exp2-2x2`: drop the bolded
   "registered"/"unregistered, exploratory" sentences → "The
   §\ref{sec:exp2} narrative focuses on the two no-documents arms (naive
   vs optimised). The two documents = yes rows per agent complete the
   2×2 factorial (\ref{sec:annex-exp2})."
2. ~L802 equalisation paragraph: keep the tentativeness, re-anchor it on
   design (N=4 agents, directional evidence), drop "unregistered and
   exploratory".
3. ~L829 Extensions opener: keep exploratory-as-post-hoc, drop the
   registration clause → "They are exploratory — performed after the
   experiments were presented; each ..."
4. ~L1206 Conclusion: "the exploratory, unregistered documents
   condition" → "the documents condition".
5. ~L1970-1984 exp2-annex italic opener: rewrite registration-free —
   four agents, N=5/cell, 2×2 factorial, 80 sessions; no-documents arms
   (40) ran first, documents arms (40) completed the factorial, reported
   jointly; F1 scored for all 80; Phase C deferred; inferential analysis
   lives in the technical report's Experiment 2 chapter. Drop the
   "registered-report write-up — registration, the H1--H6 analysis
   plan" sentence.
6. ~L2101-2107 classifier paragraph: "the registered (and earlier-run)
   choice" → "the earlier-run choice"; "the cross-vendor independence
   the registration sought when it moved off" → "the cross-vendor
   independence goal that drove the switch away from".
7. ~L2154: "The registered design has two arms" → "The no-documents
   design has two arms".
8. ~L2190-2227: retitle subsection "As-run deviations from the
   registration" → "Design notes" (`\subsection*` + matching
   \addcontentsline). Keep the three facts as plain design decisions:
   documents axis added (40→80 sessions, never aggregated with
   no-documents arms in the F1 analysis), Claude optimised-arm 0/5
   bibliography-parsability exclusion (still F1-scorable), Phase C
   deferred. Final sentence loses "registered-report treatment" and
   "locked H1--H6 plan": "The inferential analysis, per-arm validity
   criteria, and the descriptive F1/cost statistics are in the technical
   report's Experiment 2 chapter."
9. ~L2318: "all 40 registered runs" → "all 40 no-documents runs".
10. Tests: in `tests/test_manuscript_exp2_annex_as_run.py` DELETE
    `test_preregistration_named` entirely; in
    `test_factorial_framing_present` delete the "exploratory" assertion
    (keep the 2×2 check); update the `test_references_report_chapter`
    docstring ("for the registered analysis" → neutral). Same PR as the
    prose change.
11. Sweep: `grep -n -i 'regist' slides/manuscript/main.tex` must return
    only "statistical register"-family hits afterwards; sweep
    `docs/editorial-brief.md` likewise and reword entry text that says
    "unregistered/exploratory condition" to "documents condition".

## Test

- Red step: add to the exp2-annex test file a negative guard
